 4. ✈️ Trump&#x27;s catering-truck ruse 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A catering truck parked next to Air Force One before President Trump departed Ankara, Turkey, last month. Photo: Alex Brandon/AP In an elaborate operation last month, President Trump secretly swapped planes on a tarmac in Turkey through a catering truck to protect against an assassination threat from Iran, The Washington Post reports : 

 In Ankara, Trump boarded the old Air Force One jumbo jet in view of television cameras. He was secretly shuttled minutes later to a smaller plane — an Air Force C-32A — via an airport catering truck typically used to load meals and other supplies preflight, according to the U.S. official and corroborating material reviewed by The Post. That made Air Force One a "decoy" with media and some White House staff aboard, the official said. Trump had flown to the NATO summit in Turkey aboard the new Qatari-donated Air Force One jet. 

 He was set to return on the older model because of security concerns but covertly switched to a smaller plane that more often transports the vice president or Cabinet secretaries. Journalists and many White House staffers aboard Air Force One believed they were flying on the same plane as the president. 🧐 The intrigue: Instead of using the Air Force One call sign, Trump's plane used the nondescript "Reach 18."

 White House communications director Steven Cheung said in a statement : "As the President has said recently, there are many enemies of America who have their sights on him, and we use every tool at our disposal to address those threats." Keep reading (gift link). 

 
 
