 6. 🤖 Lingo: &quot;Chipflation&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Bureau of Labor Statistics via FRED . Chart: Emily Peck/Axios Memory chip prices are skyrocketing, thanks to AI demand — with no end in sight, Axios' Emily Peck writes. 

 Why it matters: "Chipflation" is pushing up prices for electronics like smartphones and laptops, as well as cloud storage and hardware costs. By the numbers: The Producer Price Index for electronic components and accessories, which measures what companies pay for semiconductor chips and other parts, has gone vertical this year — rising 27.6% in June from a year earlier.

 Keep reading . 💰 P.S. Nvidia and a group of Wall Street firms are collaborating to provide half a trillion dollars ($500 billion!) in financing to the chipmaker's customers at "attractive rates" for "the buildout of AI infrastructure over time." 

 Nvidia announced a partnership with Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs and KKR. Go deeper . 
 
