 7. ☢️ Scoop: U.S. brokers secret Syria deal 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump meets with Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa at the NATO summit in Ankara, Turkey, last month. Photo: Win McNamee/Getty Images The International Atomic Energy Agency will soon remove nuclear material from a clandestine site in Syria after the Trump administration reached a deal with Syria and Israel, Israeli and U.S. officials tell Axios' Barak Ravid . 

 According to two Israeli officials, the Assad regime stored nuclear material there that was part of its Al-Kibar nuclear reactor project. A U.S. official said the material included yellowcake, which can eventually be enriched as part of a nuclear fuel cycle. Keep reading . 

 
 
